{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured SNMPv2c monitoring from node2 to node1 using the requested read-only community. System identity, uptime, contact, and location are exposed; writes are rejected. The asset register, Ubuntu 24.04.3 release, and 6.8.0-71 kernel were preserved. Both nodes passed sequential restart and recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Installed Ubuntu-compatible Net-SNMP 5.9.4 packages: snmpd on node1 and client utilities on node2.","Restricted SNMP access to node2 and the system OID subtree.","Set sysLocation to West Branch and sysContact to ops@branch.test.","Enabled snmpd at boot and bound it to node1's managed IP on UDP/161.","Verified successful reads and explicit noAccess responses for writes.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SNMPv2c access from node2 to node1 exposes system identity and uptime","command_ids":["cmd-0492b1fd8fd54356","cmd-2d60a797ee7744eb"],"summary":"node2 successfully read sysDescr, sysUpTime, sysContact, sysName, and sysLocation before and after restarts."},{"requirement":"sysLocation and sysContact have the requested values","command_ids":["cmd-3c62d4ac25244138","cmd-0492b1fd8fd54356","cmd-2d60a797ee7744eb"],"summary":"Configuration and remote queries show West Branch and ops@branch.test."},{"requirement":"Community permits reads but rejects writes","command_ids":["cmd-0492b1fd8fd54356","cmd-14a3e42fdf1c4d2e","cmd-2d60a797ee7744eb"],"summary":"Reads succeeded; SNMP SET attempts returned noAccess, and subsequent reads confirmed values were unchanged."},{"requirement":"Asset register is preserved","command_ids":["cmd-71e8a20c83eb48d3","cmd-3c62d4ac25244138","cmd-dfa70a890eb54525","cmd-1c813a0e2a224109"],"summary":"The register remains at /srv/legacy2/snmp-readonly-monitoring/asset-register.csv with checksum da19717ac6440a3f765b43e60902dc7670b3d3ef133daa4a009a5f726fc6509a, size 65, mode 644, and root ownership."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel are retained","command_ids":["cmd-71e8a20c83eb48d3","cmd-82f08e29dd2a4232","cmd-2d60a797ee7744eb","cmd-1c813a0e2a224109"],"summary":"Both nodes remain on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-d39410a67d9b4a1a","cmd-613718cd7cde4e32","cmd-ff92b4dd17c446f0","cmd-dfa70a890eb54525","cmd-14a3e42fdf1c4d2e"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from f9bf293d-1eb8-423e-b185-84e94db646f3 to 4c4c7cf8-3c9c-4297-8103-834a1c7e42ee. snmpd, listener, remote reads, write rejection, and asset data recovered."},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-1d33be3dd61b4c23","cmd-412be4b98f904f89","cmd-7133d37580654756","cmd-2d60a797ee7744eb"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 37344ae4-6582-4c1f-ac5c-fcb32f67b968 to 6e6f5d3c-75a2-47fe-9e1d-949dbb8009be. The SNMP client and end-to-end read-only monitoring recovered."}]}
